  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Living Conditions For Displacement-Affected Populations In Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The escalation of conflict in the Occupied Palestinian Territory since October 2023 has created an unparalleled humanitarian catastrophe. As of 22 October 2025, more than 68,234 Palestinians have been killed and 170,373 injured, while over 1.9 million people-nearly 90 per cent of the population-remain displaced, often multiple times. This project builds on IOM&apos;s existing Common Pipeline Programme by enabling the procurement of shelter and hygiene supplies to support displacement-affected populations in Gaza.</narrative>
  </description>
